**One caveat you should carry forward:** the hook output in this worktree is currently `Advisor: outage (fail_open); route by hand: ...`. The stdin shape is correct — the prompt is parsed and a directive is rendered — but the advisor backend is not answering, so **the 142.14 ms median measures the fail-open path, not a healthy advisor round trip.** Treat it as a floor, and re-run this same script once the advisor is live before comparing anything against it. Also, `minMs 122.63` vs `maxMs 321.56` sits far below the 2500 ms child budget in the shim (`CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS`, shim line 20) and the 500 ms stdin deadline, so no sample was clamped by either limit.

